From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:10:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: start the server in a TaskWindow; keep the desktop
 running

RISC OS has no fork()/exec(), and a desktop program must call Wimp_Poll
regularly or every other task stops.

- New utility/fc_riscos.[ch]: output redirection, Wimp_StartTask, task
  alive check (TaskManager_TaskNameFromHandle), Message_Quit.
- connectdlg_common.c: on RISC OS, client_start_server() runs
  "TaskWindow <app dir>.freeciv-server ..." with Wimp_StartTask (the
  app dir from Freeciv$Dir, expanded by the client),
  WimpSlot from FreecivServer$WimpSlot (default 36000K); the connect
  loop stops when the TaskWindow has gone; a hard kill sends
  Message_Quit to the TaskWindow.
- fc_usleep() can be given a hook (fc_set_usleep_hook()); the SDL2
  client sets one that calls SDL_Delay(), which polls the Wimp. UnixLib's
  nanosleep() busy-waits without polling.
- gui-sdl2 main loop: select() on the server socket without a timeout
  (UnixLib's select() also waits without polling), then SDL_Delay(10)
  when no event is pending.
- Client and server heaps go in dynamic areas ("Freeciv Heap",
  "Freeciv server heap"); stdout/stderr go to the files named by
  Freeciv$Output / FreecivServer$Output (else discarded), since
  printing from a desktop task opens a command window.
